<title>SRI LANKA: Ceylon Tobacco says 1996 net up 21.6 pct.</title>
<headline>Ceylon Tobacco says 1996 net up 21.6 pct.</headline>
<dateline>COLOMBO 1997-02-26</dateline>
<text>
<p>Audited results of Ceylon Tobacco Co Ltd for the year ending 31 December, 1996.</p>
<p>(in millions of rupees unless stated):</p>
<p>			    1996		   1995</p>
<p>     Turnover	17,854.19  vs	 16,136.11</p>
<p>     Net profit	 575.22   vs	   472.95</p>
<p>     Tax provision    268.44   vs	   307.89</p>
<p>NOTE - The blue chip Ceylon Tobacco Co is a subsidiary of BAT Industries Plc and Sri Lanka's monopoly cigarette maker.</p>
<p>-- Colombo newsroom (941) 434319</p>
</text>
